      "text": [
        " قَالَ لِي أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"لَمَّا حَضَرَتْ أَبِي عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ اَلْوَفَاةُ ضَمَّنِي إِلَى صَدْرِهِ ثُمَّ قَالَ \"يَا بُنَيَّ اِصْبِرْ عَلَى اَلْحَقِّ وَ إِنْ كَانَ مُرّاً يُوَفَّ إِلَيْكَ أَجْرُكَ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ\" \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5891 - Abu Hamza Al-Thumali narrated that Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) said: \"When death approached my father (as), he embraced me to his chest and said:\n'O' my son, be patient upon the truth even if it is bitter, for your reward will be given to you without measure.'\""
        ]
      }
